The 32 teams at the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] were split into eight groups of four, labelled A–H. Group A comprised [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Croatia national football team|Croatia]], [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]] and [[Cameroon national football team|Cameroon]]. The first match was played on 12 June 2014, with the last two played concurrently on 23 June. The top two teams, Brazil and Mexico, advanced to the round of 16.

