===Brazil vs Mexico===
{{commons category|2014 FIFA World Cup Match 17, Brazil v Mexico|Brazil vs Mexico}}
The two teams had met in 38 previous matches, including three times in the FIFA World Cup group stage, all won by Brazil ([[1950 FIFA World Cup|1950]]: 4–0; [[1954 FIFA World Cup|1954]]: 5–0; [[1962 FIFA World Cup|1962]]: 2–0).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140519222312/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=24|url-status=dead|archive-date=19 May 2014|title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit|publisher=FIFA.com|page=24}}</ref> Their most recent meeting was in the [[2013 FIFA Confederations Cup]] group stage, won by Brazil [[2013 FIFA Confederations Cup Group A#Brazil v Mexico|2–0]].

Mexican goalkeeper [[Guillermo Ochoa]] made four outstanding saves to deny Brazil.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/17/brazil-mexico-world-cup-2014-group-a-match-report|title=Brazil fail to find a way past marvellous Mexico|date=17 June 2014 |work=The Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref> In the first half, he saved a header from [[Neymar]] tight to his right to push the ball around the post, and blocked a close-range effort from [[Paulinho (footballer, born July 1988)|Paulinho]]. In the second half, he saved a low shot from Neymar and a late point-blank header from [[Thiago Silva]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285134 |title=Brazil 0–0 Mexico |date=17 June 2014 |work=BBC Sport |access-date=18 June 2014 }}</ref>

This was the first time since the [[1970 FIFA World Cup]] that the host team drew 0–0 in the group stage (in the case, the own Mexico, in the opening match of the respective tournament, an [[1970 FIFA World Cup Group 1#Mexico vs Soviet Union|0-0 draw with Soviet Union]]).{{Citation needed|date=June 2014}} Mexico became the first team from outside [[UEFA]] or [[CONMEBOL]] to take a point from Brazil in the World Cup.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/world-cup-crib-notes-day-7/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190819065908/https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/world-cup-crib-notes-day-7/|url-status=dead|archive-date=19 August 2019|title=World Cup Crib Notes: Day 7|publisher=FiveThirtyEight|date=18 June 2014}}</ref>

