===Cameroon vs Croatia===
{{commons category|2014 FIFA World Cup Match 18, Cameroon v Croatia|Cameroon vs Croatia}}
The two teams had never met before.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=26|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140519222312/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=26|url-status=dead|archive-date=19 May 2014|title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit|publisher=FIFA.com|page=26}}</ref>

In a match where both teams needed at least a point to stay alive in the competition, Croatia opened scoring when [[Ivica Olić]] scored from close range from [[Ivan Perišić]]'s pass. Just before half time, Cameroon was reduced to 10 men when [[Alex Song]] was dismissed for an off the ball incident with [[Mario Mandžukić]]. Perišić scored at the beginning of the second half when he intercepted Cameroonian goalkeeper [[Charles Itandje]]'s goal kick and ran 50 yards before slotting in at the near post.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/croatia-cameroon-world-cup-group-b-match-report|title=Mario Mandzukic hits double as classy Croatia sink sorry Cameroon|date=19 June 2014 |work=The Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref> Mandžukić scored the last two goals, the first a header from [[Danijel Pranjić]]'s corner and the second a tap in after Itandje parried [[Eduardo da Silva|Eduardo]]'s shot into his path.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/10909837/Cameroon-vs-Croatia-World-Cup-2014-as-it-happened.html |title=Cameroon v Croatia, World Cup 2014: as it happened |first=Mehreen |last=Khan |work=The Telegraph |date=19 June 2014 |access-date=19 June 2014}}</ref> The result confirmed Cameroon's elimination from the tournament.

In a case of infighting, Cameroonian defender [[Benoît Assou-Ekotto]] was caught on camera head-butting teammate [[Benjamin Moukandjo]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285162|title=Cameroon 0 Croatia 4|publisher=BBC Sport|date=18 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/blogs/soccer-dirty-tackle/alex-song-elbows-mario-mandzukic-in-the-back-for-some-reason--gets-sent-off-233143661.html|title=Alex Song elbows Mario Mandzukic in the back for some reason, gets sent off|publisher=Yahoo Sports|date=18 June 2014|access-date=19 June 2014 |first=Brooks |last=Peck}}</ref> Song later apologised to Mandžukić and his country for his ejection, while Cameroonian coach [[Volker Finke]] said he was very disappointed with their performance.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.espnfc.com/fifa-world-cup/story/1893099/cameroon-coach-volker-finke-stunned-by-benoit-assou-ekotto-head-butt |title=Assou-Ekotto head-butt stuns Finke |first=Mehreen |last=Khan |work=[[ESPN]] |date=19 June 2014 |access-date=19 June 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=finke-red-card-no-reason-to-lose-it-2377068.html |title=Finke: Card no reason to see red |work=[[FIFA.com]] |date=19 June 2014 |access-date=19 June 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140622030905/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y%3D2014/m%3D6/news%3Dfinke-red-card-no-reason-to-lose-it-2377068.html |archive-date=22 June 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/world-cup-cameroon-coach-disgusting |title=World Cup: Cameroon coach slams 'disgusting' player behavior in loss |work=The Guardian |date=19 June 2014 |access-date=20 June 2014}}</ref>

On 1 July 2014, Cameroon officials announced that they had opened an investigation on claims that seven of the Cameroon's players were involved in fixing the result.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28102841|title=World Cup 2014: Cameroon investigates match-fixing claims|publisher=BBC Sport|date=1 July 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28114493|title=World Cup 2014: Match-fixer denies predicting Cameroon result|publisher=BBC Sport|date=1 July 2014}}</ref> However, FIFA said there was no evidence that there were any match fixing in any of Cameroon's matches.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/28132691|title=World Cup 2014: Fifa says no proof of Cameroon match-fixing|publisher=BBC Sport|date=2 July 2014}}</ref>

Olić, who previously scored a goal in the 2002 World Cup, became the second player to have a 12-year gap between World Cup goals, after [[Michael Laudrup]] in 1986 and 1998.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=olic-twelve-years-and-still-going-strong-2376962.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140620132828/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2014/m=6/news=olic-twelve-years-and-still-going-strong-2376962.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=20 June 2014|title=Olic: Twelve years and still going strong|publisher=FIFA.com|date=19 June 2014}}</ref> Mandžukić became the first Croatian player to score a brace in a World Cup game. The 4–0 scoreline was also the biggest win by Croatia in the World Cup.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://sunnewsonline.com/new/?p=68607 |location=Lagos, Nigeria|title=Eagles down, but not out -Ameobi |date=20 June 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714120629/http://sunnewsonline.com/new/?p=68607 |archive-date=14 July 2014 |newspaper=[[The Sun (Nigeria)|The Sun]]}}</ref>

