===Cameroon vs Brazil===
The two teams had met in four previous matches, including in the [[1994 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, won by Brazil [[1994 FIFA World Cup Group B#Brazil vs Cameroon|3–0]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=39|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140519222312/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=39|url-status=dead|archive-date=19 May 2014|title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit|publisher=FIFA.com|page=39}}</ref> Their most recent meeting was in the [[2003 FIFA Confederations Cup]] group stage, won by Cameroon 1–0. Cameroon midfielder [[Alex Song]] was suspended for the match (first match of a three-match ban), after being sent off in the previous match against Croatia.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/27975534|title=World Cup 2014: Cameroon's Alex Song given three-match ban|publisher=BBC Sport|date=23 June 2014}}</ref>

Brazil, where a draw would guarantee their qualification to the knockout stage, opened the scoring in the 17th minute when [[Luiz Gustavo]] crossed from the left for [[Neymar]] to beat the goalkeeper with a first time low side-footed finish to the corner.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/23/cameroon-brazil-world-cup-2014-match-report|title=Neymar scores twice to ease Brazil past Cameroon into final stages|date=23 June 2014|work=The Guardian|access-date=24 June 2014}}</ref> Already-eliminated Cameroon equalised when [[Allan Nyom]] beat [[Dani Alves]] on the left before crossing for [[Joël Matip]] to finish from close range. Neymar put Brazil back in front when he collected the ball from [[Marcelo (footballer, born 1988)|Marcelo]] and ran at goal before finishing with a low right foot shot that wrong footed the goalkeeper from just inside the penalty area.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/sports/worldcup/world-cup-2014-2-neymar-goals-carry-brazil-past-cameroon.html|title=Brazil Romps Past Cameroon and Into Knockout Rounds|date=23 June 2014|work=New York Times|access-date=24 June 2014}}</ref> In the second half [[David Luiz]] crossed from the left for [[Fred (footballer, born 1983)|Fred]] to extend Brazil's lead with a close range header before half-time substitute [[Fernandinho (footballer, born May 1985)|Fernandinho]] completed the scoring when he collected a pass from [[Oscar (footballer, born 1991)|Oscar]] before finishing with a low right footed shot.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25285277|title=Cameroon 1 Brazil 4|date=23 June 2014|work=BBC Sport|access-date=24 June 2014}}</ref> The result assured that Brazil pipped Mexico on goal difference to qualify to the knockout stage as group winners.

The match was Brazil's 100th in the World Cup, and they followed Germany (which played their 100th match in their first game of the 2014 World Cup) to become the second team to reach the milestone.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-soccer-world-century/neymar-scores-100th-goal-of-world-cup-in-brazils-100th-game-idUSKBN0EY2O220140623|title=Neymar scores 100th goal of World Cup in Brazil's 100th game|work=Reuters|date=23 June 2014}}</ref>

